-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",381,{
[12161]="7000F245\n1\tBring the Fashion Maven's scroll to an Outfitter\tBring the Fashion Maven's scroll to an Outfitter to exchange it for the package left for you by the Maven. Outfitters can be found in Celondim, Stock, Trestlebridge, Othrikar, Rivendell, Thorin's Hall, Michel Delving and Bree-town.\n",
[12162]="7004A381\n1\tTalk to Captain Lachír\tYou should talk to Captain Lachír in Anglach, in Udûn, to learn what will happen next.\n2\tReturn to Mulnír\tReturn to Mulnír at the Foothold\n",
[12163]="7004A8CC\n1\tPatrol the gate of Durthang in Lhingris\tThe gate of Durthang can be found on the road in Lhingris to the north of the ruined encampment. Legolas has asked you to patrol Durthang and learn what has transpired between the Orcs and spiders there.\n2\tTalk to the dying Uruk at Durthang\tThe dying Uruk can be found near the gate of Durthang in Lhingris. You have arrived to find the aftermath of a bloody battle between the warriors of Durthang and the spiders of Lhingris. An Uruk nearby with grave wounds may be able to explain what happened.\n",
[12164]="70052981\n1\tFind some sign of Honey-bell in the Beorning-lands\tHoney-bell is probably somewhere in the Beorning-lands, beyond Sterkist's sight. You should find some sign of Honey-bell's wanderings.\n2\tBring Honey-bell's bell to Sterkist\tSterkist can be found at the Beorninghús. You should show Sterkist the bell you found.\n3\tTalk to Haldis\tHaldis can be found at the Beorninghús. You should talk to Haldis about where she found Honey-bell.\n4\tGive Honey-bell a good pat\tHoney-bell can be found at the Beorninghús. You should give Honey-bell a good pat.\n5\tTalk to Sterkist\tSterkist can be found at the Beorninghús. You should talk to Sterkist.\n",
[12165]="7004186A\n1\tTravel to Lornost to the south-east of Ost Anglebed\tLornost can be found to the south-east of Anglebed across the river Sarni. Nimithil has asked you to search the sacked settlement of Lornost for any sign of survivors or the Enemy.\n2\tSinged papers can be found throughout Lornost in Lebennin. You have not found any survivors, but singed papers swirl through the air nearby. You should see if they contain any useful information.\t\n3\tSearch deeper in Lornost\tLornost can be found to the south-east of Ost Anglebed in Lebennin. You have not found any sign of survivors or the Enemy outside of a paper from the Scourge. You should continue your search deeper in Lornost.\n4\tCollect the note from the fallen man of Lornost\tThe note is speared into a man's chest in the north-western corner of Lornost in Lebennin. You have not found any survivors, but you have discovered a note on a fallen man. You should examine it before returning to Ost Anglebed.\n5\tDeliver the news of Lornost to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed\tNimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin. You have searched Lornost thoroughly and discovered the cause for its fall. You should return to Nimithil and tell her what you have learned.\n",
[12166]="7000752C\n1\tFind Aunt Prunella's umbrella\tGoblins may be found in the north-west Greenfields. If one of them took Aunt Prunella's umbrella, it might be lying somewhere inside one of their camps. You promised Fosco Boffin that you would look for his Aunt Prunella's umbrella. He fears that she ran afoul of goblins.\n2\tBring Prunella's umbrella to Fosco Boffin\tFosco Boffin is in Scary, near the centre of town. You promised Fosco Boffin that you would look for his Aunt Prunella's umbrella. He fears that she ran afoul of goblins.\n3\tTalk to Fosco Boffin\tFosco Boffin is in Scary, near the centre of town. Fosco was distressed by your recovery of his Aunt Prunella's umbrella; however, a neighbour informed him that she had actually been visiting her all day, and that Prunella had lost her umbrella earlier in the day. Fosco motions you over.\n",
[12167]="70037971\n1\tThe dissenters who separated from the party going to Helm's Deep can likely be found in Marton in the Westfold. You should search for the dissenters who separated from Agelwyn's party.\t\n2\tSearch for Egelnoth\tEgelnoth is somewhere in Marton. You should search for Egelnoth.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have discovered a bitter scene in Marton -- the death of those who defied the wisdom of their Thane.\n",
[12168]="7006422A\n1\tDefeat tomb-robbers at Rantost ([see journal]/8)\tTomb-robbers can be found at Rantost, on the northern islands of Lake Evendim. Tarneth has asked you to defeat the tomb-robbers at Rantost and see why they have begun to search the old ruins.\n2\tDefeat tomb-robbers at Rantost (8/8)\tTomb-robbers can be found at Rantost, on the northern islands of Lake Evendim. Tarneth has asked you to defeat the tomb-robbers at Rantost and see why they have begun to search the old ruins.\n3\tDeliver the strange map to Tarneth in Tinnudir\tTarneth can be found in Tinnudir, on the shores of Lake Evendim.\n4\tExamine Naegir's map\tYou should examine Naegir's map and see if you notice anything else that Tarneth missed.\n5\tTalk to Tarneth\tTarneth can be found in Tinnudir, on the shores of Lake Evendim.\n6\tSurvey Lake Evendim from Tinnudir\030Travel to Tinnudir\030Survey Lake Evendim from the Eavespires\030Travel to the Eavespires\030Survey Lake Evendim from Men Erain\030Travel to Men Erain\030Survey Lake Evendim from Tyl Ruinen\030Travel to Tyl Ruinen\tTarneth has asked you to survey Lake Evendim from several locations using her spy-glass. You should travel to Tinnudir, the Eavespires, Men Erain, and the isle of Tyl Ruinen and survey Lake Evendim. You can survey Lake Evendim near each of the dock-masters at these locations.\n7\tTalk to Tarneth\tTarneth can be found in Tinnudir, on the shores of Lake Evendim.\n8\tTalk to Tarneth and search for the wreck of the Ectheldur\tTarneth can be found in Tinnudir, on the shores of Lake Evendim.\n9\tTalk to Tarneth in Tinnudir\tTarneth can be found in Tinnudir, on the shores of Lake Evendim.\n",
[12169]="7005314B\n1\tMeet Radagast at the Gladden Fields\tRadagast can be found in the Gladden Fields. After learning of several concerning matters, Radagast has asked you to meet him in the Gladden Fields.\n2\tTalk to Radagast in the Gladden Fields\tRadagast can be found in the Gladden Fields. You have found Radagast standing on a small bluff on the marshy banks of the Anduin.\n",
[12170]="70034696\n1\tSearch the small farm for cows\tThe cows were last seen at the little farm in Dunfast. You should search the small farm to see what became of the four cows.\n2\tSearch for the fourth cow\tOne cow is missing from the farm that was overtaken by wolves. You should search near Dunfast for the missing cow.\n3\tUse the whistle to call the cow to you\tThe cow can be summoned by whistling for her. You should lead the cow to the Dunfast refugees' hideout.\n4\tLead the cow to the refugees' hideout\tThe refugees' encampment can be found south-west of Dunfast. The cow can be summoned by whistling for her. You should lead the cow to the Dunfast refugees' hideout.\n5\tTalk to the cow at the refugees' hideout\tThe cow can be summoned by whistling for her. You should talk to the cow.\n6\tTalk to Herethryth\tHerethryth is at the Dunfast refugees' hideout in the Whitshaws.\n",
[12171]="70047BC6\n1\tPlant Mílgamel's plants and the mushroom samples in the soil (total: 3)\tThe planting boxes can be found near Mílgamel in Haerondir. Mílgamel has asked you to plant the flowers and herbs she carried from Ithilien in the soil of Dagorlad you brought to Haerondir. She also wishes for you to re-plant the mushrooms in the soil.\n2\tTalk to Mílgamel at Haerondir\tMílgamel can be found at Haerondir. You have planted the various mushrooms and herbs in the soil you gathered and should now speak to Mílgamel.\n3\tWait with Mílgamel\tMílgamel is at Haerondir. Mílgamel has added a splash of the slag-water to one of the planting boxes, and has asked you to wait with her and observe the results.\n4\tTalk to Mílgamel\tMílgamel can be found at Haerondir. The slag-water ruptured the planting box and dripped into the soil at Haerondir. You should speak to Mílgamel.\n",
[12172]="70049562\n1\tTalk to Dernaith outside the Oath-taker's Horn\tDernaith can be found at the foot of the statue of Sauron near the Oath-taker's Horn in Dor Amarth. Megoril has asked you to speak to Dernaith about the fates of the dwarf-rings and their bearers.\n2\tTalk to Gimli outside the Oath-taker's Horn\tGimli can be found outside the Oath-taker's Horn in Dor Amarth. Dernaith has told you of a confrontation he had with an echo of the Dark Lord, a glamour, bound to the statue of Sauron. The glamour spoke cryptically, but told of the damned in the Mordath - the Black Pits of Mordor. You should return to Gimli and see if he has come to a decision about what is to be done about the Firehorns and King Váskmun Greytooth.\n",
[12173]="7003181B\n1\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found in the mead hall of Snowbourn. Fastred has asked you to accompany him to the site of his father's grave, where he wishes to speak to you in private.\n2\tTalk to Fastred\tFastred can be found inside the mead hall of Snowbourn. Having spoken to Fastred at his father's grave, and fended off a strange, powerful foe, you should speak to Fastred in Snowbourn.\n",
[12174]="70002EFF\n1\tLocate the father-lode and take an ore sample\tThe father-lode is somewhere to the north-west of Othrikar. Find the father in the raw rock The lode lies amongst high hills Fell falcons soar through skies and Savage lynx guard the gorges Shining the silver, glittering the gold A cliff's crags keep the secret The old records combined with the mining map suggested to Regin the location of the father-lode, but the directions were far from precise. Regin has asked you to find a suitable rock formation and take an ore sample.\n2\tTalk to Regin\030Collect Ore-sample\030Collect Mining Pick\tRegin is at Othrikar. You found a rock formation matching the description Regin compiled from the map and old records. You should bring the ore sample you took from the site back to Regin.\n",
[12175]="70068243\n1\tPick up sheaf of wheat from Gadir, the farmer\tPick up wheat from Gadir, the farmer. He can be found along the road to the Elder Hall.\n2\tPick up jugs of khôrob from Ziriha, the merchant\tPick up jugs of khôrob from Ziriha, the merchant. She can be found by the fishing pier.\n3\tPick up fish from Umaris, the fisher\tPick up fish from Umaris, the fisher. She can be found by the fishing pier.\n4\tGive all the gathered ingredients to Ekhmun, the cook\030Give sheaf of wheat to Ekhmun\030Give jugs of khôrob to Ekhmun\030Give fish to Ekhmun\tDeliver ingredients to Ekhmun, the cook. He can be found near Ziriha.\n5\tTalk to Elder Roshat about the feast\tReturn to Elder Roshat in the centre of Khûtra.\n",
[12176]="70069023\n1\tTake your place as the guest of honour\tTake your place as the guest of honour where the feast has been laid out.\n2\tListen to Elder Roshat, then cheer with him\tListen to Elder Roshat, then cheer with him.\n",
[12177]="70026EFC\n1\tTalk to Riagán to attend the Feast of the Running Stag\tYou should speak with Elder Riagán in Lhan Tarren. The Elder of the Stag-clan has looked forward to inviting you to the festival.\n2\tTalk to Elder Riagán\tElder Riagán is in Lhan Tarren. You should speak with Elder Riagán.\n",
[12178]="700576C2\n1\tComplete to receive a map to celebrate Midsummer in Minas Tirith!\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows!\n2\tComplete to receive a map to celebrate Midsummer in Minas Tirith!\tThe greatest of all Midsummer celebrations can be found in Minas Tirith! As Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows!\n",
[12179]="7003A2CC\n1\tTalk to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon can be found outside the Mead Hall in Underharrow. You have arrived at Underharrow and met with Ellen Fremedon, the settlement's acting leader. You should now speak to Ellen to learn more of her and her burdens.\n2\tTalk to Ellen Fremedon\tEllen Fremedon can be found outside the Mead Hall of Underharrow. You have spoken to Ellen Fremedon of her family and Underharrow. You should now speak to her of other matters.\n",
[12180]="70000076\n1\tFind the missing fifth gear\tThe fifth gear is in a chest in a spider lair north and east of Kheledûl in eastern Haudh Lin. Bávor has asked you to recover the fifth and final gear from a terrible spider-lair.\n2\tBring the fifth gear to Bávor\030Collect Gear\tBávor is in Thorin's Hall. Bávor will be pleased to see you have recovered the fifth and final gear.\n",
[12181]="70071637\n1\tReturn to Nashûbu\030(Optional) Use the Hamâti War-horse to quickly travel back to camp\tNumûru believes you should return to camp to assess what actions can best win the battle in Emax Dûl. You can return to Nashûbu quickly using the nearby Hamâti War-horse.\n2\tHelp Sorkamâl with 'Implements of Evil'\030Help Razâl with 'Orkish Allies'\030Help Numûru with 'Cleaning the Streets'\030Help Hanâbu with 'The Boon of Aradûn'\tYour allies at Nashûbu have requests to complete to further the war effort. You should complete quests to help win the battle in Emax Dûl.\n3\tTalk to Numûru\tYou have done much to further the war effort in Emax Dûl. You should return to Numûru in Nashûbu for instructions.\n4\tHelp Sorkamâl with 'Return to the Royal Quarter'\030Help Numûru with 'Barging into the Barracks'\030Help Razâl with 'Consuming Madness'\tYour allies at Nashûbu have requests to complete to further the war effort. You should complete quests to help win the battle in Emax Dûl.\n5\tTalk to Numûru\tYou have done much to win the battle at Emax Dûl. You should return to Numûru in Nashûbu.\n",
[12182]="70064381\n1\tYou should aid the Hill-men of Angmar and work to oppose the Iron Crown in Carn Dûm. NOTE: To advance this quest, you must complete one of the following on any group Size or difficulty Tier: 'Sant Lhoer, the Poison Gardens', 'Thaurisgar, the Vile Apothecary', 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin', or 'Gwathrenost, the Witch-king's Citadel'.\t\n2\tTalk to Muirál at Bail Avarc\tMuirál can be found at Bail Avarc in Angmar. You have done much to aid those opposing the Iron Crown at Carn Dûm. You should talk to Muirál. NOTE: Bail Avarc can initially only be accessed via stable-master routes. Bail Avarc can be reached via the stable-masters at Esteldín, Gath Forthnír, and the stables of Rivendell.\n",
[12183]="70037C84\n1\tDefeat the waves of attackers ([see journal]/8)\tDefeat the enemies assaulting the barricades and ballistae protecting the Hornburg. Aragorn will aid in the defence, but if he or the blockade fall, the Hornburg will surely be lost to your foes. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[12184]="700466D5\n1\tDefeat Shumug\tShumug can be found roaming the after-battle Pelennor. You should find and defeat the Orc captain Shumug.\n2\tTalk to Éomer\tYou should talk to Éomer, who can be found at Aragorn's pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.\n",
[12185]="70001739\n1\tChief Walraig is with his kin in Tór Gailvin, a camp north-east of Aughaire. Lore-singer Arzhur has asked you to raid the Hillman fort to the north-east. If you can defeat Chief Walraig, you may be able to forestall a war between the clans.\t\n2\tArzhur is in Aughaire, south-west of Chief Walraig's camp. You should return to Arzhur with news of your victory over Chief Walraig.\t\n",
[12186]="70067C46\n1\tDefeat Sûbodal, the Haradrim sorcerer at Grijâti\tYou are to travel south and west into the Haradrim camp of Grijâti once again. This time, however, you are seeking the sorcerer Sûbodal, one of the Haradrim leaders. You are to eliminate him and return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl when the effort is complete.\n2\tReturn to Girgish at Jax Phanâl\tThe sorcerer is slain. You should return to Girgish at Jax Phanâl and tell her of your success.\n",
[12187]="7006F091\n1\tReach the battlefield Shubârza described\tShubârza has asked that you find the sword once wielded by her brother, Iregâr, who fell in battle nearby in an Ekhamâti assault.\n2\tFind Zigûli\tYou have reached the battle-ground about which Shubârza told you. There are many weapons scattered around. One of these must be the sword once wielded by her brother, Iregâr, who fell in battle nearby in an Ekhamâti assault.\n3\tReturn to Shubârza with Zigûli\tReturn to Shubârza in Amalíbi's camp near Iridír with her brother's sword.\n",
[12188]="700169CA\n1\tDestroy gates (total: 6)\tThe track is at Athmadhul, south-east of Mekhem-bizru. Ótam wants you to return to Athmadhul, but this time wishes you to dismantle the track fences the Warg-riders use to train.\n2\tTalk to Ótam at Mekhem-bizru\tÓtam is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Athmadhul. Ótam will be pleased to hear that the training track has been destroyed.\n",
[12189]="70067CAB\n1\tCollect pelts from sekbiri on the Shield Isles ([see journal]/16)\tHunt down jungle-beasts throughout the Shield Isles. Skin their corpses, and when you have enough, return to Melitara at Halrax for payment.\n2\tDeliver the hides to Melitara\tYou collected enough pelts to meet Melitara's current demand. You should return to her at her station in Halrax.\n3\tShine the stretched hides ([see journal]/4)\tMelitara thanked you for collecting the furs and mentioned shining some previously stretched hides. She once again asked for your aid.\n4\tTalk to Melitara\tYour work on the hides is complete, and they look great. Melitara wants to speak with you.\n",
[12190]="7000EAB3\n1\tFind Nef's shield\tNef thinks he dropped his shield in Jä-rannit along the road to Itä-mâ at a junction in the roads. Nef has asked you to search for the shield he lost and return it to him.\n2\tTalk to Nef\030Collect Broken Shield\tNef is in Sûri-kylä, north from Itä-mâ along the Ice Bay. You should return Nef's shield to him at once.\n",
[12191]="700173BF\n1\tDeal with the leader of the Ghâsh-hai in the Grand Stair\030Deal with the war-host of the Ghâsh-hai within the Grand Stair\tOssur is at the Orc-watch. Ossur has tasked you with aiding him against the trolls and Ghâsh-hai of the Grand Stair.\n2\tTalk to Ossur at the Orc-watch\tOssur is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair. You should return to Ossur at the Orc-watch and inform him that the tasks set before you regarding the Ghâsh-hai are complete.\n",
[12192]="70033C8D\n1\tApproach the Grim and begin the battle.\tThe Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes.\n2\tDefeat the Grim fueling the Easterlings furnace before it explodes\tThe Easterlings have constructed a vile machine to fill the tunnels and caves of the Lonely Mountain with deadly noxious smoke and fumes. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
})
